O = {}
O['physics-carry-force-omits-hold-and-cap'] = ("Fixed as the session lead decided, with the skeptic's better fix. src/engine.js carriedHit: the hold is booked for the whole squash, uncapped (footJ = hold x T, splatWithFooting's limit as the charger's mass goes to infinity); carry.F is the squash's own force plus that hold (splat), so carry.F x carry.T = supplied; carry.hold reports the hold. The rock round the bolts keeps its tear load x T, and the page labels it an estimate ('The lab books the rock's tear-out load for the whole squash, an estimate: real rock fails once, and then the plug slides along with him'). src/app.html collideCharge: the 'Force of the hit' tile, the 'Forces at the hit' bars ('The hit: squash plus his hold', 'What holds Rex' from carry.hold) and the squash paragraph use carry.F ('pushes with about 273 kN: the squash's own 255 kN plus the 17.7 kN with which his footing holds Rex back, since Ollie can't slow. That force over that time is what Ollie's source supplies'); the 'push rises until it gives / rough' sentence is gone; the math says F = Q/s + the hold. README decision 1 and the Known limit rewritten. New figures: all-out 1.59 MN over 35 ms (supplied 55,000, unchanged); least disruptive 273 kN (was 255 kN); 1 m/s set speed: footing 11,100, supplied 14,100 kg m/s (was 6,000), force 22.4 kN; a jump onto Rex on real ground: 57,700 + 49,700 = 107,000 kg m/s (was 99,400), 2.83 MN. Checks: test/powers.js 8a (footWant = hold x T, carry.F = squash + hold and F x T = supplied to 1e-9, the 1 m/s and jump figures; 8b: the rock books tear x T); test/shots.js 'review round 1: the carried hit's force includes the hold, uncapped' (the tile, the paragraph, the bar label, 14,000 and 11,100 at 1 m/s, no 'push rises'). Reverts: E1 (the cap back) fails 8a and the page check; E2 (the force without the hold) fails 8a and the page check; P1 (the page using the squash's force) fails the page check.", ['E1-carry-hold-capped', 'E2-carry-force-without-hold', 'P1-hit-force-squash-only'])
O['physics-armwrestle-pin-loser-pad'] = ("Fixed with the skeptic's formula. src/engine.js armWrestle: with the winner's power on, the loser's pad load |holdArm m_l a - (P_l + effMass m_l a)|, a = (P_w - P_l)/(effMass (m_A + m_B)), is reported (loserPadLoad) and the table breaks in the pin ('pin') when the larger pad passes what it carries; the standing contest follows, as with the power off. Rex at the dial against Ollie at 1 t, Things keep their form off: Rex's pad 2.45 kN, Ollie's 24.2 kN against the table's 15.1 kN, so the pin breaks the table and Rex pins standing at 83 m/s (power off: Rex's pad, 249 kN, then standing at 21.8 m/s). The page's verdict names the pad that gives ('forcing it down loads Ollie's elbow pad with about 24.2 kN (what turns his forearm against Rex's hand), more than the 15.1 kN the table carries'), the item gives both pads, the math gives the formula; README decision 10, 'What changed', 'What moved' and the PR body corrected. Checks: test/powers.js 8i (each of the 2,160 grid runs: the loser's pad as computed by the test, and the table breaks in a pin exactly where the larger pad passes it; 420 runs break by the loser's pad, the skeptic's count; the 1 t example breaks by 'pin' with 24.2 kN); test/shots.js 'arm wrestling, the loser's pad breaks the table in a pin with the power on' (rewritten). Revert E4 (only the winner's pad checked) fails 8i and the page check.", ['E4-arm-loser-pad-unchecked'])
O['copy-pin-never-breaks'] = ("Fixed once with physics-armwrestle-pin-loser-pad (the same claim): the sentence 'a pin never breaks the table' is gone from the page, README decision 10, 'What changed' and the PR body, because with the loser's pad checked the pin can break the table (the session lead's decision). The item now reads '...The loser's pad still carries what turns his own forearm against the winner's hand, about 24.2 kN: that is a force on the loser, not anyone's push back, so no power takes it. That is more than the table carries, so the pin breaks it.' Check: test/shots.js 'arm wrestling, the loser's pad breaks the table in a pin with the power on' (no 'never breaks the table' on the view). Revert P16 (the old item) fails it; P16b (the old 'broke' text, naming Rex's pad) fails it too.", ['P16-arm-pad-item', 'P16b-arm-broke-text'])
O['physics-steady-push-bolted-real-rock'] = ("Fixed. src/engine.js standoff: with the pusher's power on and the one pushed bolted on real rock, past the rock's tear load (groundTear, about 697 kN) the outcome is 'forceWins' with rockGives: true, tearB, and his hold from then on his feet (HB, RB: 17.7 kN); rock = that push on the rock around his bolts. Below it (13.5 t) his bolts hold as before. The page says 'Rex is bolted, but on real rock: Ollie's push (890 kN) is more than the rock around his bolts takes (about 697 kN), so it tears out, and Rex is driven back with a plug of rock, held only by his feet (17.7 kN)...', with the chip 'Rex's rock tears loose' and the hold tile 'his feet, once the rock around his bolts tears out at about 697 kN'. Checks: test/powers.js 8f (torn at the dial, the same drive as standing; holds at 13.5 t); test/shots.js 'review round 1: a steady push past the rock's tear load tears a bolted Rex loose' (no 'his bolts hold'). Reverts: E10 (no tear) fails 8f and the page check; P6 (the page's torn verdict) fails the page check. The break-the-ground preset there (13.5 t, where the rock cracks) now names it, 'The least effort that breaks the rock around Rex's bolts', in the same check; revert P26 fails it.", ['E10-push-rock-holds', 'P6-push-torn-verdict', 'P26-push-ground-preset-what'])
O['duo-steady-push-no-harm'] = ("Fixed as the session lead decided: the one driven back is followed and judged. src/engine.js standoff: with the pusher's power on and 'forceWins', drive { d, t, vB, pB, EB, slideB, footB, relativistic } is the shoving match's shove-off (the pusher's push less the hold, a constant force, over the shorter strokes.throw, relativistic; then slideStop on his feet), and recoilAbsorbed { J: push x t } the pusher's push back (the ledger closes); an unbounded push gives just under light speed. At the default dial: 37.6 m/s, 109 m, exactly Wrestle's figures for a bolted Ollie shoving Rex off. src/app.html duoFacts (Collide push): harm 'Rex is driven back faster than sound' or 'Rex is driven back and slides X, past the nearest people'; the least disruptive effort is now 5,470 kg-force (was all-out, 'no cap needed'). The verdict adds 'Over the shove's stroke (2.44 m) that sends Rex off at 37.6 m/s, and he slides 109 m before he stops', a 'Rex is driven off at' tile and a 'Driven back' item; the presets' reason with the power on says the one pushed hands the ground a friction drag (no 'slow load'), and the ground preset says only the one pushed slides. README decision 7, What moved and Known limits updated. Checks: test/powers.js 8f (the drive equals pushMatch's shove-off to 1e-12, the ledger, unbounded at c); test/shots.js 'review round 1: the steady push follows and judges the one driven back' (ceiling 5.47 t, 'faster than sound' at unlimited strength, no 'Nothing in this test does harm', no 'slow load', the presets' reasons) and the tightened 'Collide, the steady push on and off'. Reverts: E11 (no drive) fails 8f and the page check; P5 (drive not judged) fails the page check; P23 (the old 'slow load' reason) and P24 (the old ground reason) fail it; P25 (the drive tile and item dropped) fails 'the steady push on and off'.", ['E11-push-not-followed', 'P5-push-drive-not-judged', 'P23-push-why-own', 'P24-push-ground-gap-own', 'P25-push-feet-text'])
O['copy-push-harm'] = ("Fixed once with duo-steady-push-no-harm (the same defect): the steady push's effort box no longer says nothing does harm while Rex is driven back; it judges his slide and his speed against sound (ceiling 5,470 kg-force; at unlimited strength 'At this effort Rex is driven back faster than sound'). Checks and reverts as recorded there.", ['E11-push-not-followed', 'P5-push-drive-not-judged'])
O['duo-paradox-claimed-harmless'] = ("Fixed as the session lead decided. src/app.html duoFacts flags the paradox (out.noAnswer 'the hit', out.judged 'the charge (its speed against sound) and the charger's take-off'); duoEffortBox never says 'Nothing in this test does harm', 'Even all-out, this test doesn't ...' or 'no cap needed' there: 'All-out. Nothing the lab can judge in this test does harm here ...', 'Courtesy ceiling: none that the lab can judge. The hit has no physical answer here (the canon's ruling), so the lab can't judge its harm; it judges only the charge (its speed against sound) and the charger's take-off. Even all-out, those do no harm...', and a preset never reached: '...Even all-out, those don't shatter windows 15 m away...'. Where the take-off does harm (the 10^9 kg jump) the ceiling line adds the same sentence. The same flag and wording cover the other pushes with no physical answer (the steady push, the shoving match, Both at once and standing arm wrestling at unlimited strength into bolts their power holds), and the Two-player effort card says so. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: the paradox is never called harmless...'. Reverts: P3 (no flag) and P21 (the effort box's old wording) each fail it.", ['P3-paradox-no-flag', 'P21-effortbox-harmless'])
O['copy-shovingmatch-paradox-nothing-moves'] = ("Fixed as the session lead decided (the skeptic's code, with the bolted one's push required to beat the other's hold). src/engine.js pushMatchOwn: where only one unlimited push meets bolts their power holds, that push has no physical answer (noAnswer: whose push) and moves nobody; the bolted one's own push is real, so the outcome is 'shovedOff' (winner the bolted one, contact Infinity), at just under light speed when it is unlimited; 'paradox' (nothing moves) remains only where his push can't beat the other's hold. shoveBoth likewise (noAnswer 'shove' or 'back'; the paradox only with both held or the real shove stalled). The page: 'Ollie is bolted to ground that their power holds, so Rex's unlimited push into his bolts meets a hold without limit: that push has no physical answer (the canon's ruling), and it moves nobody. Ollie's own push on Rex is real (a contest lets force move), and Rex holds only 17.7 kN, so Ollie shoves him off at just under light speed', a chip, a canon item; the effort box keeps the faster-than-sound harm and adds the no-answer sentence. At the default dial with a what-if unlimited Rex, Ollie bolted shoves Rex off at 37.6 m/s. Tests 8g ('up' is now shovedOff with noAnswer; up2 at c; upP still the paradox) and 8h (pd, po, pb) rewritten. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: one bolted at unlimited strength, the other's push has no answer but his own is real'. Reverts: E7 (the old early paradox) fails 8g and the page check; P8 (the page's verdict) fails the page check.", ['E7-pm-nothing-moves', 'P8-pm-noanswer-verdict'])
O['duo-one-sided-paradox-nothing-moves'] = ("Fixed once with copy-shovingmatch-paradox-nothing-moves (the same defect) in pushMatchOwn, and in shoveBoth: with Rex bolted on Unbreakable footing at unlimited strength, Both at once now says 'Rex is bolted to ground that their power holds, so Ollie's unlimited shove into his bolts meets a hold without limit: that shove has no physical answer (the canon's ruling), and it moves nobody. Rex's own shove on Ollie is real (a contest lets force move): Ollie leaves at just under light speed', with 'At this effort someone flies off faster than sound' back; a shover the other's shove can't move shows 'moves: not at all' instead of '0 m/s'. Checks: test/powers.js 8h; test/shots.js 'review round 1: one bolted at unlimited strength...'. Reverts: E9 (shoveBoth's old paradox) fails 8h and the page check; P9 (the page's Both at once verdict) and P20 (the 'moves' tile) fail the page check.", ['E9-both-nothing-moves', 'P9-both-noanswer-verdict', 'P20-both-moves-tile'])
O['physics-shoving-match-bolted-rock-claim'] = ("Fixed in the engine (the skeptic's better fix). src/engine.js pushMatchOwn: a single bolted wrestler on real rock is torn loose once the other's push passes the rock's tear load (groundTear, about 697 kN), at any strength (tornA/tornB, tearA/tearB N); from then on only his feet hold him (holdAfterA/B, his friction hold, also for his slide); his feet hand the ground that hold x t (the ledger closes; the rock's brief share as it tears isn't followed, stated). At the default dial with Rex bolted and Unbreakable footing off, both are now shoved apart at 26.6 m/s each; 'can't move Rex's bolts' appears only where the other's push is below the tear load, and then says 'the rock around them holds up to about 697 kN'. The Known limit is replaced. Checks: test/powers.js 8g (torn at the dial; holds at 5.47 t; the feet's share); test/shots.js 'review round 1: a single bolted wrestler's rock tears past its tear load...'. Revert E6 (the rock checked only at unlimited strength) fails 8g and the page check.", ['E6-pm-rock-unchecked-finite'])
O['copy-shovingmatch-torn-unbounded'] = ("Fixed once with physics-shoving-match-bolted-rock-claim: once his rock tears his hold is his feet's (17.7 kN) and his feet hand the ground that hold x t (7.2 x 10^-5 kg m/s each at unlimited strength, not 'unbounded'); the page shows his hold as 'the rock around his bolts, about 697 kN' and the chip 'Ollie holds 17.7 kN once his rock tears'. Checks: test/powers.js 8g (ur.footB = 17.7 kN x t, below 10^-3 kg m/s); test/shots.js 'review round 1: a single bolted wrestler's rock tears...' (no 'Ollie unbounded' or 'Ollie holds unlimited'). Reverts: E8 (the torn side's feet unbounded) fails 8g; P11 (the hold text) fails the page check.", ['E8-pm-torn-feet-unbounded', 'P11-torn-hold-unlimited'])
O['physics-from-above-bolted-real-rock'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix, without adding the bolts' tear load). src/engine.js carriedHit: rockGives only when hit from the side; landed on from above, a bolted body is driven in, bolts and all, held by the ground's bearing beyond his weight (from the friction stance holdOf builds), as standing: hold 1.52 MN, footing 57,700 kg m/s, the same depth. The page shows only 'Rex driven into the ground', the bar 'What holds Rex: the ground' and 'the ground under his feet, which bears 1.52 MN on the concrete slab (from above, his bolts go down into it with him: they could only add to that, and the lab doesn't count them)'; the Known limit names it. Checks: test/powers.js 8b (from above, bolted equals standing, rockGives false); test/shots.js 'review round 1: from above, a bolted Rex on real ground is held by the ground's bearing'. Reverts: E3 fails 8b and the page check; P2 (the hold text) and P2b (the bar) fail the page check.", ['E3-from-above-rock-tears', 'P2-from-above-hold-text', 'P2b-from-above-hold-bar'])
O['duo-arm-loser-bolts-tear'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix). src/engine.js armWrestle: with his power on, each one's bolts carry the press that reaches his body, min(AA, AB): the other's in a stalemate, the loser's in a pin. Rex at 10^6 kg against a bolted Ollie at 100 short tons, Unbreakable footing off: tearB 0.32 (222 kN), not 3.52, so no 'Ground around Ollie's bolts tears out'. Checks: test/powers.js 8i (a bolted loser's tear = his press / groundTear; equal presses each the other's); test/shots.js 'review round 1: a bolted loser's rock carries the loser's press in a standing pin'. Revert E5 (the skeptic's mutant E16) fails 8i and the page check.", ['E5-arm-tear-winners-press'])
O['duo-push-ground-preset-reason'] = ("Fixed by checking the rock (physics-shoving-match-bolted-rock-claim) and naming it: with the power on and one of them bolted, the shoving match models the ground (models.ground), so the break-the-ground preset finds 73 t, 'The least effort that tears the rock out around Rex's bolts' (src/app.html duoEffortBox's preset wording). The standing reason is kept for the power off ('Standing, their feet slide...') and reads 'Standing, the one pushed slides long before the ground under him could break' with the power on. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: a single bolted wrestler's rock tears...' (the preset's wording, no 'Standing, their feet slide'). Revert P12 (the preset wording) fails it; E6 also fails it.", ['P12-ground-preset-what', 'E6-pm-rock-unchecked-finite'])
O['duo-ratio-long-digits'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix): the ratio uses big(ratio, 2): 'about 50 times' at the default dial, 'about 560,000 times' at 10^9 kg. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: the shoving match's ratio is rounded'. Revert P10 fails it.", ['P10-ratio-digits'])
O['duo-nkb-note-energy'] = ("Fixed: the Never knocked back note and the Their powers card now say 'the motion it frees as it stops at him is taken back unless he means it (the heat it made in the air on the way stays real)'. Checks: test/shots.js 'Never knocked back: on by default...' (the note) and 'the cards for pull request 4' (the card; no 'the energy it frees where he stands is taken back'). Reverts: P17 (the note) fails the first; P18b (the card) fails the second.", ['P17-nkb-note', 'P18b-card-energy-contests'])
O['copy-nkb-note'] = ("Fixed once with duo-nkb-note-energy for the energy, and the contests are named: the note, the recoil switch's label and the Their powers card say 'In their contests (arm wrestling, every Wrestle move, Collide, the partner toss)', the Newton card the same, replacing 'every two-player test'. Checks: test/shots.js 'Never knocked back: on by default...' and 'the cards for pull request 4' (no 'every two-player test' in the page). Reverts: P17 fails the first; P18b and P18c (the Newton card) fail the second.", ['P17-nkb-note', 'P18b-card-energy-contests', 'P18c-card-newton-contests'])
O['duo-card-five-powers'] = ("Fixed: the Their powers card says 'so six powers are on unless the reader turns them off: Air resistance absorbed, Things keep their form, Unbreakable footing, They take their own recoil, Safe passenger and Never knocked back (one switch each).' Check: test/shots.js 'the cards for pull request 4'. Revert P18a fails it.", ['P18a-card-five-powers'])
