O['duo-shoving-shake-reason'] = ("Fixed by counting it (the skeptic's better fix). src/app.html duoFacts (the shoving match, the power on): where a bolted winner shoves the other off, his bolts hand the ground the loser's push over the push (his foot momentum over max(a limb's contact time, the push), the Shove tab's rule for a bolted partner's bolts): a shaking source with harm 'the push through Rex's bolts shakes the ground enough that plaster may crack 5 m away'; models.shake for one bolted. Rex bolted at a 10^6 kg dial: the plaster preset finds 125 t. duoNoModel gives no 'not a blow' reason there; where nothing goes through the bolts that way (his rock torn), the plaster preset says so ('The lab counts a push through a bolted wrestler's bolts as shaking where he shoves the other off over the stroke, a quick pulse. None goes through them that way here...'). The both-bolted reason says a steady push equal and opposite. Checks: test/shots.js 'review round 1: the push through a bolted winner's bolts shakes the ground' and the plaster sentence in 'a single bolted wrestler's rock tears...'. Reverts: P13 (no source) fails the first; P14 (the old 'not a blow' reason with one bolted) and P22 (the reason where none goes through) fail the plaster sentence in the second.", ['P13-bolts-not-shaking', 'P14-shake-why-old', 'P22-recoil-why-push'])
O['duo-mutant-survivors'] = ("Fixed with the four checks the skeptic asked for, plus engine checks. test/shots.js: (a) 'the default set speed's ceiling is the carried slide, not the hit's blast' (Rex carried at 100 m/s and 516 m away, no 'air blast'): the skeptic's mutant P10 fails it; (b) 'a Never knocked back switch turned over in place gives what a fresh load gives' (both switches clicked without a reload on the fireball case at the windows preset, compared with a fresh load, and the fireball verdict after it): mutant P4 (duoKey without the switches) still passes, because no state found makes the two-player search's result depend on the switches (in the fireball case the throw's own boom and blast come first at every preset), so P4 is equivalent in practice, as the review suspected; the check guards the in-place path anyway; (c) 'a bolted loser's rock carries the loser's press in a standing pin' and 8i's tear check: mutant E16 (= revert E5) fails both; (d) 'unequal pushes, each one's push back is his own' (Rex 890 kN, Ollie 981 kN: Rex 79,000 and Ollie 88,000 kg m/s against the engine) and 8g's unequal-push ledger: mutant E25 fails both. Also 8g: one power on and one off gives the old rule (the skeptic's E24). Not added: E32 (realUpper), P6/P7 and E27, which the skeptic didn't run and found no visible effect for.", ['M-P10-hit-blast-by-default', 'M-P4-duoKey-without-switches', 'E5-arm-tear-winners-press', 'M-E25-recoilA-uses-DB'])
O['copy-paradox-coexist'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix): the paradox item ends '...so physics has no answer here (the canon's ruling)', and the four-cases cell reads 'No answer: one of them has to give, and neither can. (For light speed into a truly immovable body, infinity / infinity: physics says those two can't exist together.)'. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: the paradox is never called harmless, and the canon case isn't two settings that can't both hold'. Revert P4 fails it.", ['P4-paradox-coexist'])
O['copy-fireball-before-split'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix): catchEnvItems shows the split for a fireball made before it reaches him where Never knocked back takes its motion back: 'Stopping it at Ollie frees 3.63 TJ (870 t TNT) where he stands. 3.44 TJ of it is heat already made in the air on the way: that is real. The rest, 192 GJ, is its motion...'. Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: the fireball made on the way gives the split'. Revert P19 fails it.", ['P19-fireball-before-gate'])
O['copy-bothatonce-shove-tile'] = ("Fixed (the skeptic's better fix): where only the other's shove moves anyone, the tile shows it ('Ollie's shove 890 kN') and the muscle chip reads that shove ('Comic mode: real muscle does better here...'). Check: test/shots.js 'review round 1: Both at once shows the shove that moves Rex'. Revert P15 fails it.", ['P15-both-tile-own-shove'])
